# prettier-plugin-astro can't parse this file: a <script is:inline define:vars={{...}}>
# tag nested inside a {enabled && (<>...</>)} conditional fragment throws
# "SyntaxError: Unexpected token, expected '}'" on the script body. Reproduced in
# isolation — removing either the outer conditional/fragment or the define:vars
# double-brace syntax makes it parse fine, but both are load-bearing here (the
# overlay must stay conditionally rendered, and define:vars is the documented way
# to pass server values into an inline script). Astro's own compiler has no issue
# with this file (astro check / build both pass) — this is purely a
# prettier-plugin-astro parser gap, not a defect in the source.
